{"base":"69e1b20c50ae67ef7400b4597ce6b237af143bf3","description":"- Add `NoLocationsForCid` error that short-circuits the fetch command\n  with an actionable hint (use `--url`, or ask a seed to `serve`) when\n  an artifact has no usable locations. Avoids the generic library-level\n  `NoLocations` error surfacing to end users with no recovery path.\n- Apply connect and idle timeouts to both transports so an offline or\n  stalled provider fails within a bounded window instead of hanging:\n  20s connect, 60s per-chunk idle. HTTP wires them through a configured\n  `ureq::Agent`; iroh enforces connect via `ConnectionPool::Options`\n  and idle via a timeout around the Downloader progress stream.\n- Refactor the iroh path onto `iroh_blobs::api::downloader::Downloader`\n  with one shared `Endpoint` + `FsStore` per download call. Previously\n  each provider bound a fresh endpoint, paying setup cost repeatedly\n  and blocking partial-progress reuse across providers. `Shuffled`\n  providers now feed a single Downloader so progress persists if a\n  provider dies mid-transfer.\n- Drop `fetch_iroh_blob` / `fetch_iroh_collection` from the public API\n  since the Downloader-based flow supersedes them and no external\n  caller used them.","oid":"b755e2561d7365eff4dc582b5e14127dbed48a37","type":"revision"}